# Packages Boswas OS v1 deliberately keeps out of the image.
#
# live-build applies *.pref.chroot files while building the chroot and removes
# them afterwards, so these pins are a build-time manifest decision and are NOT
# left on installed devices. Pin-Priority -1 means APT never installs the
# package: if a required dependency ever needs one of them, the build fails
# loudly instead of silently pulling it in.

# KDE Connect opens LAN ports 1714-1764 and pairs personal phones with the
# workstation (file/clipboard transfer). Not appropriate as a default on a
# managed device; may return later as a policy-controlled option.
Explanation: Boswas: network-exposed phone pairing service
Package: kdeconnect
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

# Plasma Discover + PackageKit provide an unmanaged software-install path.
# Software is delivered through Boswas repositories and, later, Boswas Store.
Explanation: Boswas: unmanaged software installation front-ends
Package: plasma-discover plasma-discover-common plasma-discover-backend-fwupd plasma-discover-backend-flatpak packagekit packagekit-tools
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

# Fingerprint PAM changes the authentication surface (login, sudo). Biometric
# login is a Boswas ID / policy decision, not an image default.
Explanation: Boswas: biometric PAM is a policy decision
Package: libpam-fprintd fprintd
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

# KDE Welcome Center: first-login wizard that introduces "Debian GNU/Linux",
# links to KDE community and donation pages. Boswas onboarding (company
# services, support, policies) is delivered by Boswas instead (later phase).
Explanation: Boswas: upstream first-run wizard replaced by Boswas onboarding
Package: plasma-welcome
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

# Inbound remote access is never installed by default. SSH server must be
# explicitly provisioned (docs/security/baseline.md).
Explanation: Boswas: no inbound remote access by default
Package: openssh-server
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

# cups-browsed listens on the network (UDP 631). Printing is out of scope for
# v1 alpha and will be delivered through a profile.
Explanation: Boswas: network-listening print discovery
Package: cups-browsed
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1
